; ⚠ THE SEA STARTS WHERE THE SAND ENDS. At x 500 it covered half the beach: the shore runs
; 0..1000 with its top at the waterline, so the seaward half of it was underwater and the
; brush, the bangka and the practice beat all sat in the shallows. The far edge stops short
; of the island for the same reason -- the arrival at 4460 is still in the water, which is
; where a swimmer reaches it, but the sand they climb out onto is dry.
[node name="Sea" type="Area2D" parent="GameplayPlane"]
